    "body": "### Contact Details (e.g. Tox ID or email)\n\ntox:6D1E813DD98BAB2A538D5D2B4954BCAA2C7CDC59A36DF8772AE5435535A74863EABD98ECA8C0\n\n### qTox Version\n\nv1.18.3-rc.1\n\n### Commit Hash\n\n7fe10d3647e45470f86d962468ef69d8dbb3c44c\n\n### Toxcore Version\n\n0.2.20\n\n### Qt Version\n\n6.4.2\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Start qTox\n2. Select Friend from contact list who is online\n3. Starting call by pressing green button. Button is now yellow and calling sound is there.\n4. Unfortunately Friend disconnects just right after that.\n5. After few seconds qTox properly marks Friend as offline, calling buttons are now gray\n6. [BUG is here] calling sound is still there even when Friend goes offline\n\nThank you guys from TokTok community for taking care of qTox.\n\n### Observed Behavior\n\n6. [BUG is here] calling sound is still there even when Friend goes offline\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\nCalling sound should stop when called Friend goes offline\n\n### Reproducibility\n\nAlways\n\n### Operating System\n\nLinux\n\n### Operating System version/distro/name/etc.\n\n_No response_\n\n### Relevant log output\n\n```shell\n\n```",
